-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Adam.Coff.Linker.adam - a SectionSet and its imports as a PE32+ exe
  (DESIGN sec 7, sec 11)

  Every layout fact is Microsoft's "PE Format" page (MS-DOS Stub, Signature,
  COFF File Header and its Characteristics, Optional Header: Standard
  Fields, Windows-Specific Fields, Windows Subsystem, DLL Characteristics,
  Data Directories; Section Table, Section Flags, Special Sections; The
  .idata Section, The .pdata Section, The .reloc Section). "MZ" at offset 0
  is winnt.h's IMAGE_DOS_SIGNATURE, the two bytes every image starts with.

  LinkImage   one SectionSet (one object per program until M8; objects are
              never re-read, M2.9) linked into an exe's bytes, or a dll's
              (ExeSettings.Dll, M8a: IMAGE_FILE_DLL, its base 0x180000000,
              always relocatable; the exports, sorted byte-wise, each kept
              by the link-time removal as the entry is, in an export table
              after the import tables in .rdata: the directory, the address
              table, the name pointer table, the ordinal table, the dll's
              name and the names; its data directory 0). A library an
              import names that is a static one (an archive with no short
              import) gives no DLL: the import is unbound (its symbol
              Undefined) and the library's objects that define what the
              program needs are merged into the set first
              (Adam.Coff.Foreign, the libraries in first-use order, then
              the ABI's C runtime archives, CRuntimeFacts); the code reads
              such a routine's address from a local import slot (lld's: an
              8-byte pointer in .rdata, the routine's address by an Abs64)
              as it reads a DLL routine's from its IAT slot. An object's
              `__imp_` + a name the set defines (the program's routine of
              a C name: a hook, System.HookAbi) is a local import slot
              holding that definition (lld's local import,
              CoffDefinedImport), never a DLL's slot. What the
              objects still need that a DLL exports is imported from the
              first that does, the program's @linklibrary DLLs in their
              order, then the C runtime's (CRuntimeFacts' order): `__imp_` + an export is that import's slot,
              an export's own name an import thunk (the machine's jump
              through the slot, CoffMachine.ImportThunk, in .text). Image
              sections by kind, once every symbol is bound and the
              link-time removal (SU2.7, DoRemoveUnreached) has emptied what
              the entry does not reach (a Removable section no kept
              section's relocation names; a Tombstone section's reference
              to one reads 0 and is no base relocation), in this order:
              .text (code), .rdata
              (read-only, then the import tables), .data, .bss (zeroed),
              then .rsrc when the settings ask for resources (an @exeicon's
              images and group, the @addverinfo version resource:
              Adam.Coff.Resources; its data entries' offsets made RVAs, its
              own data directory), then .reloc when an Abs64 relocation
              needs a base relocation;
              in each, the set's sections of that kind by group: a group is
              every section whose group name has the same part before its
              first '$', laid where its first section (in id order) is, its
              sections by the part after the '$' (none first), then id; each
              at its alignment, the gaps in .text filled with int3 (0xCC);
              an image section with no bytes is left out. The import tables:
              the directory table, each DLL's lookup table, the import
              address table (one block, its own data directory), the
              hint / name entries (a hint is the name's index in the DLL's
              name pointer table, Adam.Coff.Exports), the DLL names (the
              found file's name). One DLL per file found, one slot per DLL
              and name. Relocations applied: Rel32 S + A - (P + 4), Rva32
              S + A, Abs64 ImageBase + S + A and a DIR64 base relocation;
              an Import symbol's address is its IAT slot. The exception
              table (the .pdata group: Adam's section and a foreign object's
              pieces) sorted by begin address after its relocations.
              Deterministic: TimeDateStamp 0, no checksum, every list in the
              set's id order.
              ImageBase 0x140000000 (a 64 K multiple above 4 GB); with no
              Abs64 the image is fixed there (IMAGE_FILE_RELOCS_STRIPPED),
              with them it is relocatable (DYNAMIC_BASE, HIGH_ENTROPY_VA).
              Always NX_COMPAT, LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE; the GUI subsystem for
              @subsystem gui (ExeSettings.Gui), else the console one;
              OS and subsystem 6.0, 1 MB of stack and of heap reserved and
              one page of each committed; sections at the arch's page
              (CoffMachine.PageSize), raw data at 512 ("the default").

  Reported at the AST declaration that needs it (a symbol's or an import's
  node; NoPlace with no tree or no node): a symbol nothing defines (LK0001),
  a DLL built for another machine (LK0002), a routine its DLL does not
  export (LK0003); an image past the 2 GB a PE32+ image holds (LK0004,
  NoPlace); an exception table whose pieces are no run of whole entries
  (LK0006, NoPlace: a foreign .pdata); an @exeicon file that cannot be
  read or holds no icon (LK0007, at its path). LK0005 (a static library,
  before its objects were linked) is retired: its number is not reused. The
  library search and the export reading report their own EX codes at the
  import's node, the static libraries' objects their AR, OB and FO codes.
  After any report the result is empty.
  Raised (a compiler bug): no sections, machine, diagnostics or settings; an entry
  that is no symbol defined in code; a section aligned past a page; a value
  its relocation field cannot hold; a .pdata that is no whole number of its
  12-byte entries.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit Adam.Coff.Linker;

import System.SysUtils, Adam.Core.Containers, Adam.Core.Messages, Adam.Compiler.SourceText,
  Adam.Compiler.Diagnostics, Adam.Compiler.AST, Adam.Backend.Sections, Adam.Backend.Parts,
  Adam.Coff.Writer, Adam.Coff.Exports, Adam.Coff.Foreign, Adam.Coff.Resources, System.IO;

public const
  // Reported (see the header)
  ADAM_ERR_LINKER_001: string = "LK0001";   // a symbol nothing defines
  ADAM_ERR_LINKER_002: string = "LK0002";   // a DLL built for another machine
  ADAM_ERR_LINKER_003: string = "LK0003";   // a routine or variable its DLL does not export
  ADAM_ERR_LINKER_004: string = "LK0004";   // an image past 2 GB
  ADAM_ERR_LINKER_006: string = "LK0006";   // an exception table of broken pieces
  ADAM_ERR_LINKER_007: string = "LK0007";   // an @exeicon file that holds no icon
  // DoLibrary's answer for a static library (an index is 0 or more, -1 a failure)
  ADAM_LINKER_STATIC: int64 = -2;
  // The set section of the local import slots (in the .rdata group)
  ADAM_LINKER_LOCAL_IMPORTS: string = ".rdata$adam_local_imports";
  // The set section of the import thunks (in the .text group): the code a static object's
  // direct call to a C runtime DLL export reaches (DoThunk), aligned as an import slot
  ADAM_LINKER_IMPORT_THUNKS: string = ".text$adam_import_thunks";
  // A group name's separator: the part before it is the group (".text$mn" is in ".text")
  ADAM_LINKER_GROUP_MARK: string = "$";
  // Thread-local storage (DoThreadLocal, PE Format "The TLS Section"): the set sections of
  // the start and end markers (mingw-w64 tlssup's: `.tls`, suffix "", made before any
  // foreign `.tls$`, and `.tls$ZZZ`), the module's index the loader writes (in .data), the
  // callback list (a null-ended array of pointers, in .rdata) and the directory (40 bytes,
  // in .rdata, data directory 9); their symbols (the index and the directory by the names a
  // C object reaches them by)
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_START_SECTION: string = ".tls";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_END_SECTION: string = ".tls$ZZZ";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_INDEX_SECTION: string = ".data$adam_tls_index";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACKS_SECTION: string = ".rdata$adam_tls_callbacks";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_SECTION: string = ".rdata$adam_tls_used";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_START_SYMBOL: string = "_tls_start";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_END_SYMBOL: string = "_tls_end";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_INDEX_SYMBOL: string = "_tls_index";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACKS_SYMBOL: string = "__adam_tls_callbacks";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_SYMBOL: string = "_tls_used";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_INDEX_SIZE: int64 = 4;
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_POINTER_SIZE: int64 = 8;
  // The directory's fields: four addresses (raw data start, end, index, callbacks), then
  // SizeOfZeroFill and Characteristics (the raw data's alignment, IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_*)
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_ADDRESSES: int64 = 4;
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_SIZE: int64 = 40;
  // The C TLS callback list's group and its members' suffix start (M8d2: `.CRT$XL*`, C's
  // __xl_a .. __xl_z; a lib's own entry is `.CRT$XLC`, Adam.Coff.Format): each address
  // word in them joins the directory's callback list (DoThreadCallbacks)
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACK_GROUP: string = ".CRT";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACK_SUFFIX: string = "XL";
  // Raised (see the header)
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_INPUT: string = "Linker: no sections, no machine, no diagnostics, no C runtime or no settings";
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_ENTRY: string = "Linker: the entry is no symbol defined in code: ";
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_ALIGN: string = "Linker: a section aligned past a page: ";
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_FIELD: string = "Linker: a value its relocation field does not hold: ";
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_UNDEFINED: string = "Linker: a relocation to an undefined symbol: ";
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_EXPORT: string = "Linker: an export is no symbol defined in a section: ";
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_THUNK: string = "Linker: an import thunk defined apart from its symbol: ";
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_LOCAL_SLOT: string = "Linker: a local import slot defined apart from its symbol: ";
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_PDATA: string = "Linker: a .pdata that is no whole number of entries: ";
  ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_INFO: string = "Linker: an Info section handed to the linker: ";
  // MS-DOS Stub and Signature: "MZ", the signature's offset at 0x3C, "PE\0\0" right after
  // a 64-byte MS-DOS header (0x3C's 4 bytes are its last)
  ADAM_LINKER_DOS_MAGIC: int64 = 0x5A4D;
  ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_POINTER_AT: int64 = 0x3C;
  ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_AT: int64 = 64;
  ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE: int64 = 0x00004550;
  ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_SIZE: int64 = 4;
  // COFF File Header: its size and the Characteristics flags used
  ADAM_LINKER_FILE_HEADER_SIZE: int64 = 20;
  ADAM_LINKER_FILE_RELOCS_STRIPPED: int64 = 0x0001;
  ADAM_LINKER_FILE_EXECUTABLE_IMAGE: int64 = 0x0002;
  ADAM_LINKER_FILE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE: int64 = 0x0020;
  ADAM_LINKER_FILE_DLL: int64 = 0x2000;
  // Optional Header (PE32+): 24 bytes of standard fields and 88 of Windows-specific ones,
  // then 16 data directories of 8 bytes; the directories used
  ADAM_LINKER_MAGIC_PE32PLUS: int64 = 0x20B;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORIES_AT: int64 = 112;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_COUNT: int64 = 16;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_SIZE: int64 = 8;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_EXPORT: int64 = 0;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_IMPORT: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_RESOURCE: int64 = 2;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_EXCEPTION: int64 = 3;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_BASERELOC: int64 = 5;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_TLS: int64 = 9;
  ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_IAT: int64 = 12;
  // The Windows-specific values written (see the header)
  ADAM_LINKER_IMAGE_BASE: int64 = 0x140000000;
  // A dll's preferred base (lld's and link.exe's default for a 64-bit dll); a dll is always
  // relocatable, as the loader may place it anywhere
  ADAM_LINKER_DLL_IMAGE_BASE: int64 = 0x180000000;
  // The .edata Section: the export directory table's size, the export address and name
  // pointer tables' entries, an ordinal table entry, the ordinal base, the tables' alignment
  ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_DIRECTORY_SIZE: int64 = 40;
  ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ENTRY_SIZE: int64 = 4;
  ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ORDINAL_SIZE: int64 = 2;
  ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ORDINAL_BASE: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ALIGN: int64 = 4;
  ADAM_LINKER_FILE_ALIGN: int64 = 512;
  ADAM_LINKER_VERSION_MAJOR: int64 = 6;
  ADAM_LINKER_VERSION_MINOR: int64 = 0;
  ADAM_LINKER_SUBSYSTEM_WINDOWS_GUI: int64 = 2;
  ADAM_LINKER_SUBSYSTEM_WINDOWS_CUI: int64 = 3;
  ADAM_LINKER_DLL_HIGH_ENTROPY_VA: int64 = 0x0020;
  ADAM_LINKER_DLL_DYNAMIC_BASE: int64 = 0x0040;
  ADAM_LINKER_DLL_NX_COMPAT: int64 = 0x0100;
  // The stack every thread reserves (committed as it grows): 8 MB, the main thread's on
  // x86_64-linux-gnu too, so a program (the compiler at the parser's nesting bound, PR0042
  // at 256 levels, included) recurses as deep on each target
  ADAM_LINKER_STACK_RESERVE: int64 = 0x800000;
  ADAM_LINKER_HEAP_RESERVE: int64 = 0x100000;
  // "PE32+ images allow for a 64-bit address space while limiting the image size to 2 gigabytes"
  ADAM_LINKER_MAX_IMAGE: int64 = 0x80000000;
  // Section Table: an entry's size and its name's bytes
  ADAM_LINKER_SECTION_HEADER_SIZE: int64 = 40;
  ADAM_LINKER_NAME_SIZE: int64 = 8;
  // The image's sections (Special Sections), .reloc's discardable flag, and .pdata (the
  // set's section the exception table is)
  ADAM_LINKER_TEXT: string = ".text";
  ADAM_LINKER_RDATA: string = ".rdata";
  ADAM_LINKER_DATA: string = ".data";
  ADAM_LINKER_BSS: string = ".bss";
  ADAM_LINKER_TLS: string = ".tls";
  ADAM_LINKER_RELOC: string = ".reloc";
  ADAM_LINKER_PDATA: string = ".pdata";
  ADAM_LINKER_RSRC: string = ".rsrc";
  ADAM_LINKER_SCN_MEM_DISCARDABLE: int64 = 0x02000000;
  // .idata: a directory entry, a PE32+ lookup / address entry, a hint, a hint's largest value
  ADAM_LINKER_IMPORT_ENTRY_SIZE: int64 = 20;
  ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE: int64 = 8;
  ADAM_LINKER_HINT_SIZE: int64 = 2;
  ADAM_LINKER_MAX_HINT: int64 = 0xFFFF;
  // A hint / name entry and a DLL name start "on an even boundary"
  ADAM_LINKER_NAME_ALIGN: int64 = 2;
  // .pdata: an x64 entry (Begin Address, End Address, Unwind Information)
  ADAM_LINKER_PDATA_ENTRY_SIZE: int64 = 12;
  // .reloc: a block's header, an entry, the page a block covers, a block's alignment (a 32-bit
  // boundary), the DIR64 type and where it sits in an entry (the high 4 bits)
  ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_HEADER_SIZE: int64 = 8;
  ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_ENTRY_SIZE: int64 = 2;
  ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_PAGE: int64 = 4096;
  ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_ALIGN: int64 = 4;
  ADAM_LINKER_REL_BASED_DIR64: int64 = 10;
  ADAM_LINKER_REL_TYPE_SHIFT: int64 = 12;
  // int3, the fill between functions in .text
  ADAM_LINKER_CODE_FILL: int64 = 0xCC;
  // What a relocation field holds: Rel32 a signed 32-bit value, Rva32 an unsigned one; the low
  // 32 bits of a .pdata sort key (an entry's index)
  ADAM_LINKER_REL32_LOW: int64 = -2147483648;
  ADAM_LINKER_REL32_HIGH: int64 = 2147483647;
  ADAM_LINKER_RVA32_HIGH: int64 = 0xFFFFFFFF;
  ADAM_LINKER_LOW_32: int64 = 0xFFFFFFFF;

public type
  // One section of the image: its name and flags, whether its bytes are in the file, its
  // size (grown while the set's sections are laid in) and where it lands
  ImageSection = object
    SectionName: string;
    Flags: int64;
    Initialized: bool;
    Size: int64;
    VirtualAddress: int64;
    RawAt: int64;
    RawSize: int64;

    init(const ASectionName: string; const AFlags: int64; const AInitialized: bool);
    begin
      self.SectionName := ASectionName;
      self.Flags := AFlags;
      self.Initialized := AInitialized;
      self.Size := 0;
      self.VirtualAddress := 0;
      self.RawAt := 0;
      self.RawSize := 0;
    end;
  end;

  // One DLL the program imports from: the file found, the name the image gives the loader,
  // its export table, its slots in first-use order, and where its tables sit in .rdata
  ImageLibrary = object
    FilePath: string;
    DllName: string;
    Table: ref ExportTable;
    Slots: ref Int64List;
    LookupAt: int64;
    AddressAt: int64;
    NameAt: int64;

    init(const AFilePath: string; const ATable: ref ExportTable);
    begin
      self.FilePath := AFilePath;
      // The loader's name: a DLL's own file name, or the DLL an import library imports from
      self.DllName := ExtractFileName(AFilePath);
      if ATable.IsImportLibrary then
        self.DllName := ATable.DllName;
      end;
      self.Table := ATable;
      self.Slots := ref Int64List();
      self.LookupAt := 0;
      self.AddressAt := 0;
      self.NameAt := 0;
    end;
  end;

type
  // One LinkImage call (see the header)
  CoffLinker = object
    hidden FSet: ref SectionSet;
    hidden FMachine: ref CoffMachine;
    hidden FEntry: string;
    hidden FEntrySymbol: int64;
    // The symbol the TLS directory's callback list names first ("" none: DoThreadLocal)
    hidden FThreadCallback: string;
    hidden FPaths: StringArray;
    hidden FTree: ref SyntaxTree;
    hidden FDiagnostics: ref Diagnostics;
    hidden FFailed: bool;
    // What the main module asks of the image (ExeSettings); the .rsrc section's bytes (empty:
    // none, DoResources), its data entries' RVA fields, its image section's index (-1 none)
    hidden FSettings: ref ExeSettings;
    hidden FResources: ByteArray;
    hidden FResourceFields: Int64Array;
    hidden FResourceIndex: int64;
    // The DLLs: a library as written -> its index + 1, a found file (lower case) -> its index
    // + 1, and the spellings and files that failed (reported once)
    hidden FLibraries: array of ref ImageLibrary;
    hidden FLibraryOfSpelling: ref StringIdMap;
    hidden FLibraryOfFile: ref StringIdMap;
    hidden FFailedSpellings: ref StringIdMap;
    hidden FFailedFiles: ref StringIdMap;
    // The static libraries in first-use order (each file once) with the node of the import
    // that first named it; a spelling or a found file (lower case) that is one -> 1
    hidden FArchiveFiles: StringArray;
    hidden FArchiveNodes: Int64Array;
    hidden FStaticSpellings: ref StringIdMap;
    hidden FStaticFiles: ref StringIdMap;
    // The set section of the local import slots (DoLocalImport); 0 until the first
    hidden FLocalImports: int64;
    // The ABI's C runtime (CRuntimeFacts: its archives and DLLs); the set section of the
    // import thunks (DoThunk), 0 until the first
    hidden FRuntime: ref CRuntimeFacts;
    hidden FImportThunks: int64;
    // The slots (one per DLL file and name): its DLL, name, hint, and where its hint / name
    // entry and its IAT entry sit in .rdata; a slot key -> its index + 1; per import id its
    // slot (-1 after a report)
    hidden FSlotLibrary: Int64Array;
    hidden FSlotName: StringArray;
    hidden FSlotHint: Int64Array;
    hidden FSlotHintAt: Int64Array;
    hidden FSlotAddressAt: Int64Array;
    hidden FSlotOfKey: ref StringIdMap;
    hidden FImportSlot: Int64Array;
    // The image's sections in order; per set section its image section's index and its
    // offset in it; the indexes of .text, .rdata and .reloc (-1 for none)
    hidden FImage: array of ref ImageSection;
    hidden FSectionImage: Int64Array;
    hidden FSectionOffset: Int64Array;
    hidden FCodeIndex: int64;
    hidden FRdataIndex: int64;
    hidden FRelocIndex: int64;
    // The set section of the TLS directory (DoThreadLocal; 0 for none)
    hidden FTlsDirectory: int64;
    // The TLS directory's callback list section (DoThreadLocal; filled by
    // DoThreadCallbacks once every object is in the set); 0 when the link made no directory
    hidden FTlsCallbacks: int64;
    // The import tables in .rdata: the directory table, the IAT block (start and size)
    hidden FDirectoryAt: int64;
    hidden FAddressesAt: int64;
    hidden FAddressesSize: int64;
    // A dll's exports (DoExports, M8a): the names sorted byte-wise and each one's symbol; the
    // export table in .rdata (DoLayExports): its start, each name's place, the dll name's,
    // its size
    hidden FExportNames: StringArray;
    hidden FExportSymbols: Int64Array;
    hidden FExportAt: int64;
    hidden FExportNameAt: Int64Array;
    hidden FExportDllAt: int64;
    hidden FExportSize: int64;
    // Per set section: whether the image keeps it (DoRemoveUnreached, SU2.7)
    hidden FLive: BoolArray;
    // The Abs64 relocations' count and, once laid out, their RVAs in order
    hidden FSiteCount: int64;
    hidden FSites: Int64Array;
    // The headers' size, the image's size, the file's size, the file's bytes
    hidden FHeadersSize: int64;
    hidden FImageSize: int64;
    hidden FFileSize: int64;
    hidden FBytes: ByteArray;

    init(const ASet: ref SectionSet; const AMachine: ref CoffMachine; const AEntry: string;
      const AThreadCallback: string; const APaths: StringArray; const ARuntime: ref CRuntimeFacts;
      const ASettings: ref ExeSettings; const ATree: ref SyntaxTree; const ADiagnostics: ref Diagnostics);
    begin
      self.FSet := ASet;
      self.FMachine := AMachine;
      self.FEntry := AEntry;
      self.FEntrySymbol := 0;
      self.FThreadCallback := AThreadCallback;
      self.FPaths := APaths;
      self.FRuntime := ARuntime;
      self.FImportThunks := 0;
      self.FTree := ATree;
      self.FDiagnostics := ADiagnostics;
      self.FFailed := false;
      self.FSettings := ASettings;
      self.FResourceIndex := -1;
      self.FLibraryOfSpelling := ref StringIdMap();
      self.FLibraryOfFile := ref StringIdMap();
      self.FFailedSpellings := ref StringIdMap();
      self.FFailedFiles := ref StringIdMap();
      self.FStaticSpellings := ref StringIdMap();
      self.FStaticFiles := ref StringIdMap();
      self.FLocalImports := 0;
      self.FSlotOfKey := ref StringIdMap();
      self.FCodeIndex := -1;
      self.FRdataIndex := -1;
      self.FRelocIndex := -1;
      self.FTlsDirectory := 0;
      self.FTlsCallbacks := 0;
      self.FDirectoryAt := 0;
      self.FAddressesAt := 0;
      self.FAddressesSize := 0;
      self.FExportAt := 0;
      self.FExportDllAt := 0;
      self.FExportSize := 0;
      self.FSiteCount := 0;
      self.FHeadersSize := 0;
      self.FImageSize := 0;
      self.FFileSize := 0;
    end;

    // True when the AST node ANode is a variable's declaration (false with no tree or no
    // node): an import it needs is a data import
    hidden const method DoIsVariable(const ANode: int64): bool;
    begin
      if (self.FTree = nil) or (ANode = 0) then
        return false;
      end;
      return self.FTree[ANode].Kind = NodeKind.VarDecl;
    end;

    // Where the AST node ANode is: NoPlace with no tree or no node
    hidden const method DoPlace(const ANode: int64): SourcePlace;
    begin
      if (self.FTree = nil) or (ANode = 0) then
        return NoPlace();
      end;
      return self.FTree[ANode].Place;
    end;

    // Reports ACode at ANode's place; the link has failed
    hidden method DoReport(const ACode: string; const ANode: int64; const ATemplate: string;
      const AArgs: MessageArgs);
    begin
      self.FDiagnostics.Add(Severity.Error, ACode, self.DoPlace(ANode), ATemplate, AArgs);
      self.FFailed := true;
    end;

    // The library file AFile read (a DLL's export table, or an import library's imports: its
    // Machine checked) into a new library; its index, or -1 after a report at APlace / ANode.
    // A static library (an archive with no import) is recorded for Adam.Coff.Foreign (its
    // objects' Machine checked there, one by one): ADAM_LINKER_STATIC
    hidden method DoReadLibrary(const AFile: string; const APlace: SourcePlace;
      const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LTable: ref ExportTable;
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LTable := ReadLibraryTable(AFile, self.FDiagnostics, APlace);
      if LTable = nil then
        self.FFailed := true;
        return -1;
      end;
      if LTable.IsImportLibrary and (LTable.Count = 0) then
        LIndex := len(self.FArchiveFiles);
        setlength(self.FArchiveFiles, LIndex + 1);
        setlength(self.FArchiveNodes, LIndex + 1);
        self.FArchiveFiles[LIndex] := AFile;
        self.FArchiveNodes[LIndex] := ANode;
        self.FStaticFiles.Put(LowerCase(AFile), 1);
        return ADAM_LINKER_STATIC;
      end;
      if LTable.Machine <> self.FMachine.Machine then
        self.DoReport(ADAM_ERR_LINKER_002, ANode, ADAM_MSG_LINKER_MACHINE,
          NoArgs().Str(AFile).Str(HexText(LTable.Machine)).Str(HexText(self.FMachine.Machine)));
        return -1;
      end;
      LIndex := len(self.FLibraries);
      setlength(self.FLibraries, LIndex + 1);
      self.FLibraries[LIndex] := ref ImageLibrary(AFile, LTable);
      self.FLibraryOfFile.Put(LowerCase(AFile), LIndex + 1);
      return LIndex;
    end;

    // The library of the found file AFile (key AFileKey): a DLL's index or ADAM_LINKER_STATIC
    // when it was read before, else read now (DoReadLibrary); -1 after a report
    hidden method DoFileLibrary(const AFile: string; const AFileKey: string;
      const APlace: SourcePlace; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LKnown: int64;
    begin
      LKnown := self.FLibraryOfFile.Find(AFileKey);
      if LKnown > 0 then
        return LKnown - 1;
      end;
      if self.FStaticFiles.Find(AFileKey) > 0 then
        return ADAM_LINKER_STATIC;
      end;
      return self.DoReadLibrary(AFile, APlace, ANode);
    end;

    // The library the import spelled ASpelling (from the declaration ANode) comes from: found
    // by BNF sec 2's search and read the first time; a DLL's index, ADAM_LINKER_STATIC for a
    // static library, -1 when the search, the reading or the Machine failed (reported once per
    // spelling and per file)
    hidden method DoLibrary(const ASpelling: string; const ANode: int64): int64;
    var
      LKnown: int64;
      LPlace: SourcePlace;
      LFile: string;
      LFileKey: string;
    begin
      if self.FFailedSpellings.Find(ASpelling) > 0 then
        return -1;
      end;
      if self.FStaticSpellings.Find(ASpelling) > 0 then
        return ADAM_LINKER_STATIC;
      end;
      LKnown := self.FLibraryOfSpelling.Find(ASpelling);
      if LKnown > 0 then
        return LKnown - 1;
      end;
      LPlace := self.DoPlace(ANode);
      LFile := FindLibrary(ASpelling, self.FPaths, self.FDiagnostics, LPlace);
      LFileKey := LowerCase(LFile);
      if (LFile = "") or (self.FFailedFiles.Find(LFileKey) > 0) then
        self.FFailed := true;
        self.FFailedSpellings.Put(ASpelling, 1);
        return -1;
      end;
      LKnown := self.DoFileLibrary(LFile, LFileKey, LPlace, ANode);
      if LKnown = ADAM_LINKER_STATIC then
        self.FStaticSpellings.Put(ASpelling, 1);
        return ADAM_LINKER_STATIC;
      end;
      if LKnown < 0 then
        self.FFailedFiles.Put(LFileKey, 1);
        self.FFailedSpellings.Put(ASpelling, 1);
        return -1;
      end;
      self.FLibraryOfSpelling.Put(ASpelling, LKnown + 1);
      return LKnown;
    end;

    // A new slot for ALibrary's export AName at AIndex in its name pointer table; its index
    hidden method DoNewSlot(const ALibrary: int64; const AName: string; const AIndex: int64): int64;
    var
      LSlot: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := len(self.FSlotName);
      setlength(self.FSlotLibrary, LSlot + 1);
      setlength(self.FSlotName, LSlot + 1);
      setlength(self.FSlotHint, LSlot + 1);
      self.FSlotLibrary[LSlot] := ALibrary;
      self.FSlotName[LSlot] := AName;
      // A hint is a 16-bit field: past it, 0 (the loader's binary search finds the name)
      self.FSlotHint[LSlot] := 0;
      if AIndex <= ADAM_LINKER_MAX_HINT then
        self.FSlotHint[LSlot] := AIndex;
      end;
      self.FLibraries[ALibrary].Slots.Add(LSlot);
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // A new pointer in the local imports section (made the first time) holding the address of
    // ARoutine (Abs64: a base relocation); its offset there
    hidden method DoLocalSlot(const ARoutine: int64): int64;
    var
      LSection: ref Section;
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      if self.FLocalImports = 0 then
        self.FLocalImports := self.FSet.AddSection(ADAM_LINKER_LOCAL_IMPORTS, SectionKind.ReadOnly,
          ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE);
      end;
      LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(self.FLocalImports);
      LAt := LSection.Size();
      LSection.PutZeros(ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE);
      self.FSet.AddReloc(self.FLocalImports, LAt, RelocKind.Abs64, ARoutine, 0);
      return LAt;
    end;

    // A local import slot (lld's for an import a static object defines): the unbound import's
    // symbol ASlot placed at a new pointer holding the address of ARoutine (DoLocalSlot). The
    // code's indirect call through the slot is the one an IAT slot takes
    hidden method DoLocalImport(const ASlot: int64; const ARoutine: int64);
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := self.DoLocalSlot(ARoutine);
      self.FSet.PlaceSymbol(ASlot, self.FLocalImports, LAt);
    end;

    // The import AId's slot (made the first time its DLL file and name are met); -1 after a
    // report, or for an import of a static library or of an external clause naming no
    // library (unbound, a local import slot made: an object defines the routine)
    hidden method DoImportSlot(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LImport: ref SectionImport;
      LLibrary: int64;
    begin
      LImport := self.FSet.ImportAt(AId);
      // `external;` names no library (BNF sec 3): the link binds the name as it binds any
      // undefined one (a static library's object, the C runtime), else LK0001 at the
      // declaration; there is no library to search
      if LImport.Library = "" then
        self.DoLocalImport(LImport.Symbol, self.FSet.UnbindImport(AId));
        return -1;
      end;
      LLibrary := self.DoLibrary(LImport.Library, LImport.Node);
      if LLibrary = ADAM_LINKER_STATIC then
        self.DoLocalImport(LImport.Symbol, self.FSet.UnbindImport(AId));
        return -1;
      end;
      if LLibrary < 0 then
        return -1;
      end;
      return self.DoSlotIn(LLibrary, LImport);
    end;

    // The slot of AImport in the DLL ALibrary (made the first time its DLL file and name are
    // met); -1 after a report
    hidden method DoSlotIn(const ALibrary: int64; const AImport: ref SectionImport): int64;
    var
      LKey: string;
      LSlot: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LKey := LowerCase(self.FLibraries[ALibrary].FilePath) + "|" + AImport.ImportName;
      LSlot := self.FSlotOfKey.Find(LKey);
      if LSlot > 0 then
        return LSlot - 1;
      end;
      LIndex := self.FLibraries[ALibrary].Table.IndexOf(AImport.ImportName);
      if LIndex < 0 then
        // an external variable's import is its data import (M8d2): named as a variable
        if self.DoIsVariable(AImport.Node) then
          self.DoReport(ADAM_ERR_LINKER_003, AImport.Node, ADAM_MSG_LINKER_VAR_NOT_EXPORTED,
            NoArgs().Str(AImport.ImportName).Str(self.FLibraries[ALibrary].FilePath));
        else
          self.DoReport(ADAM_ERR_LINKER_003, AImport.Node, ADAM_MSG_LINKER_NOT_EXPORTED,
            NoArgs().Str(AImport.ImportName).Str(self.FLibraries[ALibrary].FilePath));
        end;
        return -1;
      end;
      LSlot := self.DoNewSlot(ALibrary, AImport.ImportName,
        self.FLibraries[ALibrary].Table.HintAt(LIndex));
      self.FSlotOfKey.Put(LKey, LSlot + 1);
      return LSlot;
    end;

    // The slot of every import from id AFirst on, in import id order
    hidden method DoImportsFrom(const AFirst: int64);
    var
      LId: int64;
    begin
      setlength(self.FImportSlot, self.FSet.ImportCount);
      for LId := AFirst to self.FSet.ImportCount - 1 do
        self.FImportSlot[LId] := self.DoImportSlot(LId);
      end;
    end;

    // Every library the build names beside its imports (the set's @linklibrary names, BNF
    // sec 2) found and read as an import's library is: a static library joins the archives
    // after those the imports named (a library that needs another names it, so the needing
    // one comes first, as on lld's command line), a DLL is imported with no routine (its
    // descriptor makes the loader load it). Not found: reported at the directive's argument
    hidden method DoLinkLibraries();
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FSet.LinkLibraries) - 1 do
        self.DoLibrary(self.FSet.LinkLibraries[LI], self.FSet.LinkLibraryNodes[LI]);
      end;
    end;

    // The C runtime's archives (FRuntime) added to AForeign after the program's static
    // libraries, each found by BNF sec 2's search and reported at the node of the import
    // that first named a static library; one the program named itself is not added twice.
    // False after a report
    hidden method DoRuntimeArchives(const AForeign: ref ForeignLinker): bool;
    var
      LI: int64;
      LFile: string;
      LNode: int64;
    begin
      LNode := self.FArchiveNodes[0];
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FRuntime.Archives) - 1 do
        LFile := FindLibrary(self.FRuntime.Archives[LI], self.FPaths, self.FDiagnostics,
          self.DoPlace(LNode));
        if LFile = "" then
          self.FFailed := true;
          return false;
        end;
        if self.FStaticFiles.Find(LowerCase(LFile)) = 0 then
          if not AForeign.AddArchive(LFile, LNode) then
            self.FFailed := true;
            return false;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The static libraries' objects the program needs merged into the set (Adam.Coff.Foreign:
    // the libraries in first-use order, each read at the node of the import that first named
    // it, then the C runtime's archives); nothing when no import named one. False after
    // their report
    hidden method DoForeign(): bool;
    var
      LForeign: ref ForeignLinker;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if len(self.FArchiveFiles) = 0 then
        return true;
      end;
      self.DoStandIns();
      LForeign := ref ForeignLinker(self.FSet, self.FMachine, self.FTree, self.FDiagnostics);
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FArchiveFiles) - 1 do
        if not LForeign.AddArchive(self.FArchiveFiles[LI], self.FArchiveNodes[LI]) then
          self.FFailed := true;
          return false;
        end;
      end;
      if not self.DoRuntimeArchives(LForeign) then
        return false;
      end;
      if not LForeign.Run() then
        self.FFailed := true;
        return false;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // The C runtime's stand-ins (FRuntime.CNames / StandIns, M8d) bound before any static
    // library's object is pulled in: each C name no object defines yet defined where its
    // stand-in is, when the program holds the stand-in (its runtime unit), so a C library's
    // call reaches the runtime's routine, never a C archive's member for that name; the
    // runtime's objects define only their own names (an Adam lib in a C program keeps the C
    // runtime's)
    hidden method DoStandIns();
    var
      LStandIn: int64;
      LName: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FRuntime.CNames) - 1 do
        LStandIn := self.FSet.FindSymbol(self.FRuntime.StandIns[LI]);
        LName := self.FSet.FindSymbol(self.FRuntime.CNames[LI]);
        if (LStandIn <> 0) and (self.FSet.SymbolAt(LStandIn).Kind = SymbolKind.Defined) and
          ((LName = 0) or (self.FSet.SymbolAt(LName).Kind <> SymbolKind.Defined)) then
          self.FSet.DefineSymbol(self.FRuntime.CNames[LI], self.FSet.SymbolAt(LStandIn).SectionId,
            self.FSet.SymbolAt(LStandIn).Offset, self.FSet.SymbolAt(LStandIn).Node);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The Undefined symbol AId (named AName, first needed at ANode) defined as an import
    // thunk: the machine's indirect jump (CoffMachine.ImportThunk) through the slot of a new
    // import of AName from the C runtime DLL spelled ASpelling, so a static object's direct
    // call reaches the DLL's export, as lld's thunk does
    hidden method DoThunk(const AId: int64; const AName: string; const ASpelling: string;
      const ANode: int64);
    var
      LSlot: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
      LAt: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      LSlot := self.FSet.ImportSymbol(ASpelling, AName, ANode);
      if self.FImportThunks = 0 then
        self.FImportThunks := self.FSet.AddSection(ADAM_LINKER_IMPORT_THUNKS, SectionKind.Code,
          ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE);
      end;
      LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(self.FImportThunks);
      LAt := AlignUp(LSection.Size(), ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE);
      LSection.PutZeros(LAt - LSection.Size());
      for LK := 0 to len(self.FMachine.ImportThunk) - 1 do
        LSection.Put8(uint64(self.FMachine.ImportThunk[LK]));
      end;
      // The definition keeps the Undefined symbol's id: every relocation to it reaches the thunk
      if self.FSet.DefineSymbol(AName, self.FImportThunks, LAt, ANode) <> AId then
        raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_THUNK + AName);
      end;
      self.FSet.AddReloc(self.FImportThunks, LAt + self.FMachine.ImportThunkField, RelocKind.Rel32,
        LSlot, 0);
    end;

    // The Undefined symbol AId bound to the DLL ALibrary (spelled ASpelling: one the program
    // names, or the C runtime's) when it exports its name: `__imp_` + an export becomes that import's slot (SectionSet.BindImport:
    // the object reads the address there), an export's own name an import thunk (DoThunk);
    // else it stays
    hidden method DoRuntimeName(const AId: int64; const ALibrary: int64;
      const ASpelling: string);
    var
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
      LTable: ref ExportTable;
      LPrefix: int64;
      LBase: string;
    begin
      LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(AId);
      LTable := self.FLibraries[ALibrary].Table;
      LPrefix := len(ADAM_COFF_IMPORT_PREFIX);
      if StartsStr(ADAM_COFF_IMPORT_PREFIX, LSymbol.SymbolName) then
        LBase := Substring(LSymbol.SymbolName, LPrefix, len(LSymbol.SymbolName) - LPrefix);
        if LTable.IndexOf(LBase) >= 0 then
          self.FSet.BindImport(AId, ASpelling, LBase, LSymbol.Node);
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if LTable.IndexOf(LSymbol.SymbolName) >= 0 then
        self.DoThunk(AId, LSymbol.SymbolName, ASpelling, LSymbol.Node);
      end;
    end;

    // Every Undefined symbol among the set's first ACount bound to the C runtime DLL spelled
    // ASpelling when it exports the name (DoRuntimeName); the DLL is found the first time a
    // name needs it, so a DLL no name needs is never read. False when it could not be found
    // or read (DoLibrary reported it)
    hidden method DoRuntimeLibrary(const ASpelling: string; const ACount: int64): bool;
    var
      LId: int64;
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
      LLibrary: int64;
    begin
      LLibrary := -1;
      for LId := 1 to ACount - 1 do
        LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LId);
        if LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Undefined then
          if LLibrary = -1 then
            LLibrary := self.DoLibrary(ASpelling, LSymbol.Node);
            if LLibrary < 0 then
              return false;
            end;
          end;
          self.DoRuntimeName(LId, LLibrary, ASpelling);
        end;
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // After the static libraries, before the C runtime's DLLs: every Undefined `__imp_` + a
    // name the set defines defined at a local import slot holding that definition
    // (CoffDefinedImport, DoLocalSlot; lld's local import), so a static object reading a
    // name's address through its slot reaches the program's routine of that name (a hook,
    // System.HookAbi), never the DLL's export
    hidden method DoDefinedImports();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
      LDefined: int64;
      LName: string;
      LNode: int64;
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LCount := self.FSet.SymbolCount;
      for LId := 1 to LCount - 1 do
        LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LId);
        if LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Undefined then
          LDefined := CoffDefinedImport(self.FSet, LSymbol.SymbolName);
          if LDefined <> 0 then
            // The name and node first: the slot's section may grow the set's lists
            LName := LSymbol.SymbolName;
            LNode := LSymbol.Node;
            LAt := self.DoLocalSlot(LDefined);
            // The definition keeps the Undefined symbol's id: every relocation to it reaches
            // the slot
            if self.FSet.DefineSymbol(LName, self.FLocalImports, LAt, LNode) <> LId then
              raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_LOCAL_SLOT + LName);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // Every Undefined symbol among the set's first ACount bound to the DLL the program names
    // ASpelling (an @linklibrary, read by DoLinkLibraries) when it exports the name
    // (DoRuntimeName); a static library or one that failed (reported) binds nothing
    hidden method DoProgramLibrary(const ASpelling: string; const ANode: int64;
      const ACount: int64);
    var
      LId: int64;
      LLibrary: int64;
    begin
      LLibrary := self.DoLibrary(ASpelling, ANode);
      if LLibrary < 0 then
        return;
      end;
      for LId := 1 to ACount - 1 do
        if self.FSet.SymbolAt(LId).Kind = SymbolKind.Undefined then
          self.DoRuntimeName(LId, LLibrary, ASpelling);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // After the static libraries: every Undefined symbol bound to the first DLL that exports
    // it, the program's own first (its @linklibrary DLLs in their order, DoProgramLibrary: a
    // static library's objects call what they export, SDL3's user32 / ole32 / setupapi; lld
    // searches the command line's import libraries before the default ones), then the C
    // runtime's (CRuntimeFacts' order, DoRuntimeLibrary); the new imports given their slots.
    // Nothing when the program named no static library (its own undefined names stay LK0001)
    hidden method DoCRuntime();
    var
      LFirst: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      if len(self.FArchiveFiles) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LFirst := self.FSet.ImportCount;
      // The names the static libraries left; the thunks' own symbols come after them
      LCount := self.FSet.SymbolCount;
      for LK := 0 to len(self.FSet.LinkLibraries) - 1 do
        self.DoProgramLibrary(self.FSet.LinkLibraries[LK], self.FSet.LinkLibraryNodes[LK], LCount);
      end;
      for LK := 0 to len(self.FRuntime.LibraryNames) - 1 do
        if not self.DoRuntimeLibrary(self.FRuntime.LibraryNames[LK], LCount) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      self.DoImportsFrom(LFirst);
    end;

    // Every Undefined symbol reported at the node that needs it
    hidden method DoUndefined();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
    begin
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SymbolCount - 1 do
        LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LId);
        if LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Undefined then
          self.DoReport(ADAM_ERR_LINKER_001, LSymbol.Node, ADAM_MSG_LINKER_UNDEFINED,
            NoArgs().Str(LSymbol.SymbolName));
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The entry: a symbol defined in a code section; raises otherwise
    hidden method DoEntry();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
    begin
      LId := self.FSet.FindSymbol(self.FEntry);
      if LId = 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_ENTRY + self.FEntry);
      end;
      LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LId);
      if LSymbol.Kind <> SymbolKind.Defined then
        raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_ENTRY + self.FEntry);
      end;
      if self.FSet.SectionAt(LSymbol.SectionId).Kind <> SectionKind.Code then
        raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_ENTRY + self.FEntry);
      end;
      self.FEntrySymbol := LId;
    end;

    // Section AId kept (FLive) and put on the work stack AStack (ATop entries used), when
    // it is not kept yet
    hidden method DoKeep(const AId: int64; var AStack: Int64Array; var ATop: int64);
    begin
      if self.FLive[AId] then
        return;
      end;
      self.FLive[AId] := true;
      AStack[ATop] := AId;
      ATop := ATop + 1;
    end;

    // Link-time removal (SU2.7, Adam.Backend.Sections): every section that is not
    // Removable is kept, so is the entry's; a kept section keeps the sections it goes with
    // (their Associate it) and, unless it is a Tombstone one, the section of every Defined
    // symbol its relocations name (the TLS callback list keeps the thread callback); every
    // other section is removed (emptied). An Import symbol is a slot, no section
    hidden method DoRemoveUnreached();
    var
      LCount: int64;
      LStack: Int64Array;
      LTop: int64;
      LFirst: Int64Array;
      LNext: Int64Array;
      LId: int64;
      LChild: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
    begin
      LCount := self.FSet.SectionCount;
      setlength(self.FLive, LCount);
      setlength(LStack, LCount);
      setlength(LFirst, LCount);
      setlength(LNext, LCount);
      for LId := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        self.FLive[LId] := false;
        LFirst[LId] := 0;
        LNext[LId] := 0;
      end;
      // Each section's associated ones as a list: LFirst[A] its first, LNext the next
      for LId := 1 to LCount - 1 do
        LChild := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).Associate;
        if LChild <> 0 then
          LNext[LId] := LFirst[LChild];
          LFirst[LChild] := LId;
        end;
      end;
      LTop := 0;
      for LId := 1 to LCount - 1 do
        if not self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).Removable then
          self.DoKeep(LId, LStack, LTop);
        end;
      end;
      self.DoKeep(self.FSet.SymbolAt(self.FEntrySymbol).SectionId, LStack, LTop);
      // a dll's exports are reached from outside it (M8a)
      for LR := 0 to len(self.FExportSymbols) - 1 do
        self.DoKeep(self.FSet.SymbolAt(self.FExportSymbols[LR]).SectionId, LStack, LTop);
      end;
      while LTop > 0 do
        LTop := LTop - 1;
        LId := LStack[LTop];
        LChild := LFirst[LId];
        while LChild <> 0 do
          self.DoKeep(LChild, LStack, LTop);
          LChild := LNext[LChild];
        end;
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        if not LSection.Tombstone then
          for LR := 0 to LSection.RelocCount - 1 do
            LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LSection.RelocAt(LR).Symbol);
            if LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Defined then
              self.DoKeep(LSymbol.SectionId, LStack, LTop);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LId := 1 to LCount - 1 do
        if not self.FLive[LId] then
          self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).Remove();
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // True when AReloc of the kept section ASection is tombstoned: ASection is a Tombstone
    // one and AReloc names a Defined symbol in a removed section; its field then reads 0
    // and it is no base relocation (DoRemoveUnreached)
    hidden const method DoTombstoned(const ASection: ref Section; const AReloc: ref SectionReloc): bool;
    var
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
    begin
      if not ASection.Tombstone then
        return false;
      end;
      LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(AReloc.Symbol);
      return (LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Defined) and (not self.FLive[LSymbol.SectionId]);
    end;

    // The PE TLS pieces (see ADAM_LINKER_TLS_*), made before any foreign object joins the set
    // when the program has thread-local data, a thread callback (FThreadCallback) or reaches
    // the index symbol (a C object's thread-local variable reaches it too): the start and end
    // markers around every `.tls` group member, the index (Data, zero: the loader writes it),
    // the callback list (filled by DoThreadCallbacks once every object is in the set: the
    // loader calls each as a thread starts and ends), the directory (its
    // addresses Abs64 relocations, so each is a base relocation; its Characteristics the raw
    // data's alignment) whose section FTlsDirectory names for data directory 9. Nothing
    // when the index or the directory is defined already: the program's own
    hidden method DoThreadLocal();
    var
      LNeeded: bool;
      LAlign: int64;
      LLog: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LSymbol: int64;
      LStart: int64;
      LEnd: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LCallbacks: int64;
      LDirectory: int64;
      LTargets: Int64Array;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      LNeeded := self.FThreadCallback <> "";
      LAlign := 1;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        if self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).Kind = SectionKind.ThreadLocal then
          LNeeded := true;
          if self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).Align > LAlign then
            LAlign := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).Align;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      LSymbol := self.FSet.FindSymbol(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_INDEX_SYMBOL);
      if LSymbol <> 0 then
        if self.FSet.SymbolAt(LSymbol).Kind = SymbolKind.Defined then
          return;
        end;
        LNeeded := true;
      end;
      LSymbol := self.FSet.FindSymbol(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_SYMBOL);
      if (LSymbol <> 0) and (self.FSet.SymbolAt(LSymbol).Kind = SymbolKind.Defined) then
        return;
      end;
      if not LNeeded then
        return;
      end;
      LStart := self.FSet.AddSection(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_START_SECTION, SectionKind.ThreadLocal, 1);
      setlength(LTargets, ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_ADDRESSES);
      LTargets[0] := self.FSet.DefineSymbol(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_START_SYMBOL, LStart, 0, 0);
      LEnd := self.FSet.AddSection(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_END_SECTION, SectionKind.ThreadLocal, 1);
      LTargets[1] := self.FSet.DefineSymbol(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_END_SYMBOL, LEnd, 0, 0);
      LIndex := self.FSet.AddSection(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_INDEX_SECTION, SectionKind.Data,
        ADAM_LINKER_TLS_INDEX_SIZE);
      self.FSet.SectionAt(LIndex).PutZeros(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_INDEX_SIZE);
      LTargets[2] := self.FSet.DefineSymbol(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_INDEX_SYMBOL, LIndex, 0, 0);
      // The callback list: filled once every object is in the set (DoThreadCallbacks)
      LCallbacks := self.FSet.AddSection(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACKS_SECTION, SectionKind.ReadOnly,
        ADAM_LINKER_TLS_POINTER_SIZE);
      self.FTlsCallbacks := LCallbacks;
      LTargets[3] := self.FSet.DefineSymbol(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACKS_SYMBOL, LCallbacks, 0, 0);
      self.FSet.MakeInternal(LTargets[0]);
      self.FSet.MakeInternal(LTargets[1]);
      self.FSet.MakeInternal(LTargets[3]);
      LDirectory := self.FSet.AddSection(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_SECTION, SectionKind.ReadOnly,
        ADAM_LINKER_TLS_POINTER_SIZE);
      // The four addresses, SizeOfZeroFill (0: every byte is in the raw data), then the
      // alignment 2^LLog as (LLog + 1) in the alignment bits
      self.FSet.SectionAt(LDirectory).PutZeros(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_POINTER_SIZE *
        ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_ADDRESSES + 4);
      LLog := 0;
      while (int64(1) shl LLog) < LAlign do
        LLog := LLog + 1;
      end;
      self.FSet.SectionAt(LDirectory).Put32(uint64((LLog + 1) shl ADAM_COFF_SCN_ALIGN_SHIFT));
      for LK := 0 to ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_ADDRESSES - 1 do
        self.FSet.AddReloc(LDirectory, ADAM_LINKER_TLS_POINTER_SIZE * LK, RelocKind.Abs64,
          LTargets[LK], 0);
      end;
      LSymbol := self.FSet.DefineSymbol(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_SYMBOL, LDirectory, 0, 0);
      self.FTlsDirectory := LDirectory;
    end;

    // The TLS directory's callback list (DoThreadLocal's section, M8d2), once every object
    // is in the set: the program's thread callback first (an Abs64 to it), then every
    // address word of the `.CRT$XL*` group's sections (ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACK_*: a lib's
    // entry naming its runtime's thread callback, a C object's own) in suffix order, equal
    // suffixes in id order, each callback once (a lib's entry naming the callback the
    // program lists already is that one: an Adam host and its libs share one runtime), those
    // sections emptied (their words are the list's now), then the null that ends the list.
    // Nothing when the link made no directory (the program's own lists that group itself)
    hidden method DoThreadCallbacks();
    var
      LSuffixes: StringArray;
      LListed: Int64Array;
      LAddends: Int64Array;
      LSection: ref Section;
      LReloc: ref SectionReloc;
      LCount: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LS: int64;
      LR: int64;
    begin
      if self.FTlsCallbacks = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LCount := 0;
      if self.FThreadCallback <> "" then
        self.DoAddCallback(self.FSet.ReferSymbol(self.FThreadCallback, 0), 0, LListed, LAddends);
      end;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        if self.DoIsCallbackSection(LId) then
          setlength(LSuffixes, LCount + 1);
          LSuffixes[LCount] := self.DoSuffixOf(self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).GroupName);
          LCount := LCount + 1;
        end;
      end;
      SortStrings(LSuffixes);
      for LS := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        // A suffix met before (a run of equal ones) was walked with its first
        if (LS = 0) or (LSuffixes[LS] <> LSuffixes[LS - 1]) then
          for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
            if self.DoIsCallbackSection(LId) and
              (self.DoSuffixOf(self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).GroupName) = LSuffixes[LS]) then
              LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
              for LR := 0 to LSection.RelocCount - 1 do
                LReloc := LSection.RelocAt(LR);
                if LReloc.Kind = RelocKind.Abs64 then
                  self.DoAddCallback(LReloc.Symbol, LReloc.Addend, LListed, LAddends);
                end;
              end;
              LSection.Remove();
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      self.FSet.SectionAt(self.FTlsCallbacks).PutZeros(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_POINTER_SIZE);
    end;

    // True when the section AId is a member of the C TLS callback list's group
    // (ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACK_GROUP, a suffix starting ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACK_SUFFIX)
    // with bytes in it
    hidden const method DoIsCallbackSection(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LSection: ref Section;
    begin
      LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(AId);
      return (LSection.Size() > 0) and
        (self.DoGroupOf(LSection.GroupName) = ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACK_GROUP) and
        StartsStr(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_CALLBACK_SUFFIX, self.DoSuffixOf(LSection.GroupName));
    end;

    // The callback ASymbol + AAddend added to the TLS callback list (an Abs64 word at its
    // end) unless AListed / AAddends hold it already (each callback runs once)
    hidden method DoAddCallback(const ASymbol: int64; const AAddend: int64;
      var AListed: Int64Array; var AAddends: Int64Array);
    var
      LSection: ref Section;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to len(AListed) - 1 do
        if (AListed[LI] = ASymbol) and (AAddends[LI] = AAddend) then
          return;
        end;
      end;
      LI := len(AListed);
      setlength(AListed, LI + 1);
      setlength(AAddends, LI + 1);
      AListed[LI] := ASymbol;
      AAddends[LI] := AAddend;
      LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(self.FTlsCallbacks);
      LAt := LSection.Size();
      LSection.PutZeros(ADAM_LINKER_TLS_POINTER_SIZE);
      self.FSet.AddReloc(self.FTlsCallbacks, LAt, RelocKind.Abs64, ASymbol, AAddend);
    end;

    // The VA offset of the image section the Defined symbol ASymbol is laid in (its
    // section's; the image's end for one left out): a SecRel32's base
    hidden const method DoImageStartOf(const ASymbol: int64): int64;
    var
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LIndex := self.FSectionImage[self.FSet.SymbolAt(ASymbol).SectionId];
      if LIndex >= len(self.FImage) then
        return self.FImageSize;
      end;
      return self.FImage[LIndex].VirtualAddress;
    end;

    // Appends AImage to the image when it holds bytes (one with none is left out)
    hidden method DoAppend(const AImage: ref ImageSection);
    var
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      if AImage.Size = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LIndex := len(self.FImage);
      setlength(self.FImage, LIndex + 1);
      self.FImage[LIndex] := AImage;
    end;

    // AImage's index in the image; -1 when it was left out
    hidden const method DoIndexOf(const AImage: ref ImageSection): int64;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FImage) - 1 do
        if self.FImage[LI] = AImage then
          return LI;
        end;
      end;
      return -1;
    end;

    // The set's section AId laid into AImage at its alignment (the index AImage will have, or
    // would have, recorded for it); raises for an alignment past a page
    hidden method DoLayOne(const AImage: ref ImageSection; const AId: int64);
    var
      LSection: ref Section;
    begin
      LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(AId);
      if LSection.Align > self.FMachine.PageSize then
        raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_ALIGN + LSection.SectionName + " " + IntToStr(LSection.Align));
      end;
      AImage.Size := AlignUp(AImage.Size, LSection.Align);
      self.FSectionImage[AId] := len(self.FImage);
      self.FSectionOffset[AId] := AImage.Size;
      AImage.Size := AImage.Size + LSection.Size();
    end;

    // The group AGroupName is in: its part before the first '$' (all of it with none)
    hidden const method DoGroupOf(const AGroupName: string): string;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := IndexOf(ADAM_LINKER_GROUP_MARK, AGroupName, 0);
      if LAt < 0 then
        return AGroupName;
      end;
      return Substring(AGroupName, 0, LAt);
    end;

    // AGroupName's order within its group: its part after the first '$' ("" with none)
    hidden const method DoSuffixOf(const AGroupName: string): string;
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := IndexOf(ADAM_LINKER_GROUP_MARK, AGroupName, 0);
      if LAt < 0 then
        return "";
      end;
      return Substring(AGroupName, LAt + 1, len(AGroupName) - LAt - 1);
    end;

    // The sections of AKind in the group AGroup laid into AImage (see the header): by suffix
    // (SortStrings: none first, then byte order), equal suffixes in id order; each marked in
    // ALaid
    hidden method DoLayGroup(const AImage: ref ImageSection; const AKind: SectionKind;
      const AGroup: string; var ALaid: BoolArray);
    var
      LSuffixes: StringArray;
      LId: int64;
      LS: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
    begin
      LCount := 0;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        if (LSection.Kind = AKind) and (self.DoGroupOf(LSection.GroupName) = AGroup) then
          setlength(LSuffixes, LCount + 1);
          LSuffixes[LCount] := self.DoSuffixOf(LSection.GroupName);
          LCount := LCount + 1;
        end;
      end;
      SortStrings(LSuffixes);
      for LS := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        // A suffix met before (a run of equal ones) was laid with its first
        if (LS = 0) or (LSuffixes[LS] <> LSuffixes[LS - 1]) then
          for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
            LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
            if (LSection.Kind = AKind) and (not ALaid[LId]) and
              (self.DoGroupOf(LSection.GroupName) = AGroup) and
              (self.DoSuffixOf(LSection.GroupName) = LSuffixes[LS]) then
              self.DoLayOne(AImage, LId);
              ALaid[LId] := true;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The set's sections of AKind laid into AImage by group (see the header): each group where
    // its first section in id order is
    hidden method DoLayIn(const AImage: ref ImageSection; const AKind: SectionKind);
    var
      LId: int64;
      LLaid: BoolArray;
      LSection: ref Section;
    begin
      setlength(LLaid, self.FSet.SectionCount);
      for LId := 0 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LLaid[LId] := false;
      end;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        if (LSection.Kind = AKind) and (not LLaid[LId]) then
          self.DoLayGroup(AImage, AKind, self.DoGroupOf(LSection.GroupName), LLaid);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The import tables laid into the end of .rdata (see the header): the directory table,
    // the lookup tables, the IAT block, the hint / name entries, the DLL names
    hidden method DoLayTables(const AImage: ref ImageSection);
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LL: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LLibrary: ref ImageLibrary;
    begin
      LAt := AlignUp(AImage.Size, ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE);
      self.FDirectoryAt := LAt;
      // One entry per DLL and the null entry that ends the table
      LAt := AlignUp(LAt + ADAM_LINKER_IMPORT_ENTRY_SIZE * (len(self.FLibraries) + 1),
        ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE);
      // Each DLL's lookup table, then its address table, each ended by a null entry
      for LL := 0 to len(self.FLibraries) - 1 do
        self.FLibraries[LL].LookupAt := LAt;
        LAt := LAt + ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE * (self.FLibraries[LL].Slots.Count + 1);
      end;
      self.FAddressesAt := LAt;
      setlength(self.FSlotAddressAt, len(self.FSlotName));
      for LL := 0 to len(self.FLibraries) - 1 do
        LLibrary := self.FLibraries[LL];
        LLibrary.AddressAt := LAt;
        for LK := 0 to LLibrary.Slots.Count - 1 do
          self.FSlotAddressAt[LLibrary.Slots.Items[LK]] := LAt + ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE * LK;
        end;
        LAt := LAt + ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE * (LLibrary.Slots.Count + 1);
      end;
      self.FAddressesSize := LAt - self.FAddressesAt;
      setlength(self.FSlotHintAt, len(self.FSlotName));
      for LSlot := 0 to len(self.FSlotName) - 1 do
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, ADAM_LINKER_NAME_ALIGN);
        self.FSlotHintAt[LSlot] := LAt;
        LAt := LAt + ADAM_LINKER_HINT_SIZE + len(self.FSlotName[LSlot]) + 1;
      end;
      for LL := 0 to len(self.FLibraries) - 1 do
        LAt := AlignUp(LAt, ADAM_LINKER_NAME_ALIGN);
        self.FLibraries[LL].NameAt := LAt;
        LAt := LAt + len(self.FLibraries[LL].DllName) + 1;
      end;
      AImage.Size := LAt;
    end;

    // A dll's exports (M8a, ExeSettings.Exports) sorted byte-wise (the order the loader's
    // binary search over the name pointer table compares in), each with its symbol; raises
    // for an export no section defines (the Driver names only the main module's own
    // routines and variables: a compiler bug)
    hidden method DoExports();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if not self.FSettings.Dll then
        return;
      end;
      self.FExportNames := self.FSettings.Exports;
      SortStrings(self.FExportNames);
      setlength(self.FExportSymbols, len(self.FExportNames));
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FExportNames) - 1 do
        LId := self.FSet.FindSymbol(self.FExportNames[LI]);
        if (LId = 0) or (self.FSet.SymbolAt(LId).Kind <> SymbolKind.Defined) then
          raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_EXPORT + self.FExportNames[LI]);
        end;
        self.FExportSymbols[LI] := LId;
      end;
    end;

    // A dll's export table laid at the end of AImage (.rdata, after the import tables): the
    // export directory table, the export address table, the name pointer table, the ordinal
    // table, then the dll's name and each export's name, each ended by a zero byte (PE Format
    // "The .edata Section"); written by DoExportTable once every section has its RVA
    hidden method DoLayExports(const AImage: ref ImageSection);
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LCount := len(self.FExportNames);
      LAt := AlignUp(AImage.Size, ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ALIGN);
      self.FExportAt := LAt;
      LAt := LAt + ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_DIRECTORY_SIZE + 2 * ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ENTRY_SIZE * LCount +
        ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ORDINAL_SIZE * LCount;
      self.FExportDllAt := LAt;
      LAt := LAt + len(self.FSettings.DllName) + 1;
      setlength(self.FExportNameAt, LCount);
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        self.FExportNameAt[LI] := LAt;
        LAt := LAt + len(self.FExportNames[LI]) + 1;
      end;
      self.FExportSize := LAt - self.FExportAt;
      AImage.Size := LAt;
    end;

    // How many Abs64 relocations the set holds (each a base relocation; a tombstoned one,
    // whose field reads 0, is none)
    hidden const method DoCountSites(): int64;
    var
      LId: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
      LCount: int64;
    begin
      LCount := 0;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        for LR := 0 to LSection.RelocCount - 1 do
          if (LSection.RelocAt(LR).Kind = RelocKind.Abs64) and
            (not self.DoTombstoned(LSection, LSection.RelocAt(LR))) then
            LCount := LCount + 1;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LCount;
    end;

    // The image's sections, in order (see the header)
    hidden method DoPlan();
    var
      LImage: ref ImageSection;
    begin
      setlength(self.FSectionImage, self.FSet.SectionCount);
      setlength(self.FSectionOffset, self.FSet.SectionCount);
      LImage := ref ImageSection(ADAM_LINKER_TEXT, ADAM_COFF_SCN_CNT_CODE |
        ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_EXECUTE | ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_READ, true);
      self.DoLayIn(LImage, SectionKind.Code);
      self.DoAppend(LImage);
      self.FCodeIndex := self.DoIndexOf(LImage);
      LImage := ref ImageSection(ADAM_LINKER_RDATA, ADAM_COFF_SCN_CNT_INITIALIZED_DATA |
        ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_READ, true);
      self.DoLayIn(LImage, SectionKind.ReadOnly);
      if len(self.FLibraries) > 0 then
        self.DoLayTables(LImage);
      end;
      if self.FSettings.Dll then
        self.DoLayExports(LImage);
      end;
      self.DoAppend(LImage);
      self.FRdataIndex := self.DoIndexOf(LImage);
      LImage := ref ImageSection(ADAM_LINKER_DATA, ADAM_COFF_SCN_CNT_INITIALIZED_DATA |
        ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_READ | ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_WRITE, true);
      self.DoLayIn(LImage, SectionKind.Data);
      self.DoAppend(LImage);
      // The TLS directory's raw data: every thread's starting copy (DoThreadLocal)
      LImage := ref ImageSection(ADAM_LINKER_TLS, ADAM_COFF_SCN_CNT_INITIALIZED_DATA |
        ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_READ | ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_WRITE, true);
      self.DoLayIn(LImage, SectionKind.ThreadLocal);
      self.DoAppend(LImage);
      LImage := ref ImageSection(ADAM_LINKER_BSS, ADAM_COFF_SCN_CNT_UNINITIALIZED_DATA |
        ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_READ | ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_WRITE, false);
      self.DoLayIn(LImage, SectionKind.Zeroed);
      self.DoAppend(LImage);
      // The resources (DoResources), after the data as Microsoft's linker lays them
      if len(self.FResources) > 0 then
        LImage := ref ImageSection(ADAM_LINKER_RSRC, ADAM_COFF_SCN_CNT_INITIALIZED_DATA |
          ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_READ, true);
        LImage.Size := len(self.FResources);
        self.DoAppend(LImage);
        self.FResourceIndex := self.DoIndexOf(LImage);
      end;
      self.FSiteCount := self.DoCountSites();
      if self.FSiteCount > 0 then
        // Its size is known once the others are placed (DoLayout); 1 keeps it in the list
        LImage := ref ImageSection(ADAM_LINKER_RELOC, ADAM_COFF_SCN_CNT_INITIALIZED_DATA |
          ADAM_COFF_SCN_MEM_READ | ADAM_LINKER_SCN_MEM_DISCARDABLE, true);
        LImage.Size := 1;
        self.DoAppend(LImage);
        self.FRelocIndex := self.DoIndexOf(LImage);
      end;
    end;

    // The RVA the set's section AId starts at; one in an image section left out (it holds no
    // bytes) starts where the next image section does, or at the image's end
    hidden const method DoSectionRva(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LIndex := self.FSectionImage[AId];
      if LIndex >= len(self.FImage) then
        return self.FImageSize;
      end;
      return self.FImage[LIndex].VirtualAddress + self.FSectionOffset[AId];
    end;

    // The file offset the bytes of the set's section AId start at (a section with bytes is
    // in an image section that has them)
    hidden const method DoSectionFile(const AId: int64): int64;
    begin
      return self.FImage[self.FSectionImage[AId]].RawAt + self.FSectionOffset[AId];
    end;

    // The RVA of every Abs64 relocation's field, ascending, into FSites
    hidden method DoGatherSites();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
      LReloc: ref SectionReloc;
      LCount: int64;
    begin
      setlength(self.FSites, self.FSiteCount);
      LCount := 0;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        for LR := 0 to LSection.RelocCount - 1 do
          LReloc := LSection.RelocAt(LR);
          if (LReloc.Kind = RelocKind.Abs64) and (not self.DoTombstoned(LSection, LReloc)) then
            self.FSites[LCount] := self.DoSectionRva(LId) + LReloc.Offset;
            LCount := LCount + 1;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      SortInt64s(self.FSites);
    end;

    // The base relocation blocks of FSites (one per 4 KB page that has a site, each padded to
    // a 32-bit boundary with an IMAGE_REL_BASED_ABSOLUTE entry, zero bytes): their size, and
    // written at the file offset AAt when AWrite
    hidden method DoBaseRelocs(const AAt: int64; const AWrite: bool): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LPage: int64;
      LBlock: int64;
      LEntry: int64;
    begin
      LAt := 0;
      LI := 0;
      while LI < len(self.FSites) do
        LPage := self.FSites[LI] & (0 - ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_PAGE);
        // LJ: the first site past this page (or past the last site)
        LJ := LI + 1;
        while LJ < len(self.FSites) do
          if (self.FSites[LJ] & (0 - ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_PAGE)) <> LPage then
            leave;
          end;
          LJ := LJ + 1;
        end;
        LBlock := AlignUp(ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_HEADER_SIZE + ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_ENTRY_SIZE * (LJ - LI),
          ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_ALIGN);
        if AWrite then
          PutLe(self.FBytes, AAt + LAt, uint64(LPage), 4);
          PutLe(self.FBytes, AAt + LAt + 4, uint64(LBlock), 4);
          for LK := LI to LJ - 1 do
            // The type in the high 4 bits, the offset in the page in the low 12
            LEntry := (ADAM_LINKER_REL_BASED_DIR64 shl ADAM_LINKER_REL_TYPE_SHIFT) |
              (self.FSites[LK] - LPage);
            PutLe(self.FBytes, AAt + LAt + ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_HEADER_SIZE +
              ADAM_LINKER_BLOCK_ENTRY_SIZE * (LK - LI), uint64(LEntry), 2);
          end;
        end;
        LAt := LAt + LBlock;
        LI := LJ;
      end;
      return LAt;
    end;

    // Every image section's RVA and file place, at the page and at 512 (see the header); the
    // .reloc section sized once the sections before it are placed; LK0004 past 2 GB
    hidden method DoLayout();
    var
      LRva: int64;
      LFile: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LImage: ref ImageSection;
    begin
      self.FHeadersSize := AlignUp(ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_AT + ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_SIZE +
        ADAM_LINKER_FILE_HEADER_SIZE + ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORIES_AT +
        ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_SIZE * ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_COUNT +
        ADAM_LINKER_SECTION_HEADER_SIZE * len(self.FImage), ADAM_LINKER_FILE_ALIGN);
      LRva := AlignUp(self.FHeadersSize, self.FMachine.PageSize);
      LFile := self.FHeadersSize;
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FImage) - 1 do
        LImage := self.FImage[LI];
        if LI = self.FRelocIndex then
          self.DoGatherSites();
          LImage.Size := self.DoBaseRelocs(0, false);
        end;
        LImage.VirtualAddress := LRva;
        if LImage.Initialized then
          LImage.RawAt := LFile;
          LImage.RawSize := AlignUp(LImage.Size, ADAM_LINKER_FILE_ALIGN);
          LFile := LFile + LImage.RawSize;
        end;
        LRva := AlignUp(LRva + LImage.Size, self.FMachine.PageSize);
      end;
      self.FImageSize := LRva;
      self.FFileSize := LFile;
      if self.FImageSize > ADAM_LINKER_MAX_IMAGE then
        self.DoReport(ADAM_ERR_LINKER_004, 0, ADAM_MSG_LINKER_TOO_BIG,
          NoArgs().Str(IntToStr(self.FImageSize)).Str(IntToStr(ADAM_LINKER_MAX_IMAGE)));
      end;
    end;

    // The RVA the symbol ASymbol stands for: a Defined one's place, an Import's IAT slot
    hidden const method DoSymbolRva(const ASymbol: int64): int64;
    var
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
    begin
      LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(ASymbol);
      // Every Undefined symbol was reported, and nothing is linked after a report
      if LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Undefined then
        raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_UNDEFINED + LSymbol.SymbolName);
      end;
      if LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Import then
        return self.FImage[self.FRdataIndex].VirtualAddress +
          self.FSlotAddressAt[self.FImportSlot[LSymbol.ImportId]];
      end;
      return self.DoSectionRva(LSymbol.SectionId) + LSymbol.Offset;
    end;

    // The bytes of AText at the file offset AAt (its ending zero byte is already there)
    hidden method DoPutText(const AAt: int64; const AText: string);
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to len(AText) - 1 do
        self.FBytes[AAt + LI] := uint8(AText[LI]);
      end;
    end;

    // AValue into the ACount bytes at AAt; raises when it is outside ALow .. AHigh
    hidden method DoPutChecked(const AAt: int64; const AValue: int64; const ALow: int64;
      const AHigh: int64; const ACount: int64);
    begin
      if (AValue < ALow) or (AValue > AHigh) then
        raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_FIELD + IntToStr(AValue) + " at file offset " + IntToStr(AAt));
      end;
      PutLe(self.FBytes, AAt, uint64(AValue), ACount);
    end;

    // The data directory AIndex: ARva and ASize
    hidden method DoDirectory(const AIndex: int64; const ARva: int64; const ASize: int64);
    var
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LAt := ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_AT + ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_SIZE + ADAM_LINKER_FILE_HEADER_SIZE +
        ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORIES_AT + ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_SIZE * AIndex;
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt, uint64(ARva), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 4, uint64(ASize), 4);
    end;

    // The MS-DOS header's two fields, the signature, the COFF file header
    hidden method DoFileHeader();
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LFlags: int64;
    begin
      PutLe(self.FBytes, 0, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_DOS_MAGIC), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_POINTER_AT, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_AT), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_AT, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE), 4);
      LAt := ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_AT + ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_SIZE;
      LFlags := ADAM_LINKER_FILE_EXECUTABLE_IMAGE | ADAM_LINKER_FILE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE;
      if self.FSettings.Dll then
        LFlags := LFlags | ADAM_LINKER_FILE_DLL;
      end;
      if (self.FSiteCount = 0) and not self.FSettings.Dll then
        LFlags := LFlags | ADAM_LINKER_FILE_RELOCS_STRIPPED;
      end;
      // Machine, NumberOfSections; TimeDateStamp and the symbol table's fields stay 0
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt, uint64(self.FMachine.Machine), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 2, uint64(len(self.FImage)), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 16, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORIES_AT +
        ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_SIZE * ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_COUNT), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 18, uint64(LFlags), 2);
    end;

    // The sizes the optional header sums (code, initialized data, uninitialized data), each
    // as the image sections' file-aligned sizes
    hidden const method DoSizeOf(const ACode: bool; const AInitialized: bool): int64;
    var
      LI: int64;
      LTotal: int64;
      LImage: ref ImageSection;
      LIsCode: bool;
    begin
      LTotal := 0;
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FImage) - 1 do
        LImage := self.FImage[LI];
        LIsCode := (LImage.Flags & ADAM_COFF_SCN_CNT_CODE) <> 0;
        if (LIsCode = ACode) and (LImage.Initialized = AInitialized) then
          LTotal := LTotal + AlignUp(LImage.Size, ADAM_LINKER_FILE_ALIGN);
        end;
      end;
      return LTotal;
    end;

    // The optional header's standard and Windows-specific fields (zero fields left as they are)
    hidden method DoOptionalHeader();
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LDll: int64;
      LBaseOfCode: int64;
    begin
      LAt := ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_AT + ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_SIZE + ADAM_LINKER_FILE_HEADER_SIZE;
      LDll := ADAM_LINKER_DLL_NX_COMPAT;
      if (self.FSiteCount > 0) or self.FSettings.Dll then
        LDll := LDll | ADAM_LINKER_DLL_DYNAMIC_BASE | ADAM_LINKER_DLL_HIGH_ENTROPY_VA;
      end;
      LBaseOfCode := 0;
      if self.FCodeIndex >= 0 then
        LBaseOfCode := self.FImage[self.FCodeIndex].VirtualAddress;
      end;
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_MAGIC_PE32PLUS), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 4, uint64(self.DoSizeOf(true, true)), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 8, uint64(self.DoSizeOf(false, true)), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 12, uint64(self.DoSizeOf(false, false)), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 16, uint64(self.DoSymbolRva(self.FEntrySymbol)), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 20, uint64(LBaseOfCode), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 24, uint64(self.DoImageBase()), 8);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 32, uint64(self.FMachine.PageSize), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 36, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_FILE_ALIGN), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 40, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_VERSION_MAJOR), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 42, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_VERSION_MINOR), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 48, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_VERSION_MAJOR), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 50, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_VERSION_MINOR), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 56, uint64(self.FImageSize), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 60, uint64(self.FHeadersSize), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 68, uint64(self.DoSubsystem()), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 70, uint64(LDll), 2);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 72, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_STACK_RESERVE), 8);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 80, uint64(self.FMachine.PageSize), 8);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 88, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_HEAP_RESERVE), 8);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 96, uint64(self.FMachine.PageSize), 8);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 108, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_COUNT), 4);
    end;

    // The section table: each image section's name, sizes, places and flags
    hidden method DoSectionTable();
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LImage: ref ImageSection;
    begin
      LAt := ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_AT + ADAM_LINKER_SIGNATURE_SIZE + ADAM_LINKER_FILE_HEADER_SIZE +
        ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORIES_AT + ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_SIZE * ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_COUNT;
      for LI := 0 to len(self.FImage) - 1 do
        LImage := self.FImage[LI];
        self.DoPutText(LAt, LImage.SectionName);
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + ADAM_LINKER_NAME_SIZE, uint64(LImage.Size), 4);
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 12, uint64(LImage.VirtualAddress), 4);
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 16, uint64(LImage.RawSize), 4);
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 20, uint64(LImage.RawAt), 4);
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt + 36, uint64(LImage.Flags), 4);
        LAt := LAt + ADAM_LINKER_SECTION_HEADER_SIZE;
      end;
    end;

    // The set's bytes copied into their image sections; .text first filled with int3
    hidden method DoSectionBytes();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
      LText: ref ImageSection;
    begin
      if self.FCodeIndex >= 0 then
        LText := self.FImage[self.FCodeIndex];
        for LK := 0 to LText.Size - 1 do
          self.FBytes[LText.RawAt + LK] := uint8(ADAM_LINKER_CODE_FILL);
        end;
      end;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        if (LSection.Kind <> SectionKind.Zeroed) and (LSection.Size() > 0) then
          LAt := self.DoSectionFile(LId);
          for LK := 0 to LSection.Size() - 1 do
            self.FBytes[LAt + LK] := LSection.Bytes[LK];
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The import tables' bytes (see DoLayTables) and their two data directories
    hidden method DoImportTables();
    var
      LBase: int64;
      LRva: int64;
      LEntry: int64;
      LL: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LSlot: int64;
      LThunk: uint64;
      LLibrary: ref ImageLibrary;
    begin
      LBase := self.FImage[self.FRdataIndex].RawAt;
      LRva := self.FImage[self.FRdataIndex].VirtualAddress;
      for LL := 0 to len(self.FLibraries) - 1 do
        LLibrary := self.FLibraries[LL];
        // Import Lookup Table RVA, Name RVA, Import Address Table RVA (the stamp and the
        // forwarder chain stay 0)
        LEntry := LBase + self.FDirectoryAt + ADAM_LINKER_IMPORT_ENTRY_SIZE * LL;
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LEntry, uint64(LRva + LLibrary.LookupAt), 4);
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LEntry + 12, uint64(LRva + LLibrary.NameAt), 4);
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LEntry + 16, uint64(LRva + LLibrary.AddressAt), 4);
        for LK := 0 to LLibrary.Slots.Count - 1 do
          // By name: bit 63 clear, the hint / name entry's RVA below it
          LThunk := uint64(LRva + self.FSlotHintAt[LLibrary.Slots.Items[LK]]);
          PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + LLibrary.LookupAt + ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE * LK, LThunk, 8);
          PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + LLibrary.AddressAt + ADAM_LINKER_THUNK_SIZE * LK, LThunk, 8);
        end;
        self.DoPutText(LBase + LLibrary.NameAt, LLibrary.DllName);
      end;
      for LSlot := 0 to len(self.FSlotName) - 1 do
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + self.FSlotHintAt[LSlot], uint64(self.FSlotHint[LSlot]), 2);
        self.DoPutText(LBase + self.FSlotHintAt[LSlot] + ADAM_LINKER_HINT_SIZE,
          self.FSlotName[LSlot]);
      end;
      self.DoDirectory(ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_IMPORT, LRva + self.FDirectoryAt,
        ADAM_LINKER_IMPORT_ENTRY_SIZE * (len(self.FLibraries) + 1));
      self.DoDirectory(ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_IAT, LRva + self.FAddressesAt, self.FAddressesSize);
    end;

    // The image's preferred base: a dll's (ADAM_LINKER_DLL_IMAGE_BASE) or an exe's
    hidden const method DoImageBase(): int64;
    begin
      if self.FSettings.Dll then
        return ADAM_LINKER_DLL_IMAGE_BASE;
      end;
      return ADAM_LINKER_IMAGE_BASE;
    end;

    // A dll's export table (DoLayExports' places) and its data directory: the directory's
    // Name RVA (the dll's name), Ordinal Base, the two tables' counts and RVAs (Characteristics,
    // TimeDateStamp and the version stay 0: deterministic); each address entry the RVA of its
    // export's symbol, each ordinal its own index (the name and address tables share one order)
    hidden method DoExportTable();
    var
      LBase: int64;
      LRva: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LAddresses: int64;
      LNames: int64;
      LOrdinals: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBase := self.FImage[self.FRdataIndex].RawAt;
      LRva := self.FImage[self.FRdataIndex].VirtualAddress;
      LCount := len(self.FExportNames);
      LAddresses := self.FExportAt + ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_DIRECTORY_SIZE;
      LNames := LAddresses + ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ENTRY_SIZE * LCount;
      LOrdinals := LNames + ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ENTRY_SIZE * LCount;
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + self.FExportAt + 12, uint64(LRva + self.FExportDllAt), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + self.FExportAt + 16, uint64(ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ORDINAL_BASE), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + self.FExportAt + 20, uint64(LCount), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + self.FExportAt + 24, uint64(LCount), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + self.FExportAt + 28, uint64(LRva + LAddresses), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + self.FExportAt + 32, uint64(LRva + LNames), 4);
      PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + self.FExportAt + 36, uint64(LRva + LOrdinals), 4);
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + LAddresses + ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ENTRY_SIZE * LI,
          uint64(self.DoSymbolRva(self.FExportSymbols[LI])), 4);
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + LNames + ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ENTRY_SIZE * LI,
          uint64(LRva + self.FExportNameAt[LI]), 4);
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LBase + LOrdinals + ADAM_LINKER_EXPORT_ORDINAL_SIZE * LI, uint64(LI), 2);
        self.DoPutText(LBase + self.FExportNameAt[LI], self.FExportNames[LI]);
      end;
      self.DoPutText(LBase + self.FExportDllAt, self.FSettings.DllName);
      self.DoDirectory(ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_EXPORT, LRva + self.FExportAt, self.FExportSize);
    end;

    // Every relocation applied to its field (see the header)
    hidden method DoRelocate();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
      LReloc: ref SectionReloc;
      LSite: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LTarget: int64;
    begin
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        for LR := 0 to LSection.RelocCount - 1 do
          LReloc := LSection.RelocAt(LR);
          LSite := self.DoSectionRva(LId) + LReloc.Offset;
          LAt := self.DoSectionFile(LId) + LReloc.Offset;
          // A tombstoned field reads 0, its addend dropped with its target
          if self.DoTombstoned(LSection, LReloc) then
            PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt, 0, RelocWidth(LReloc.Kind));
            skip;
          end;
          LTarget := self.DoSymbolRva(LReloc.Symbol) + LReloc.Addend;
          match LReloc.Kind of
            RelocKind.Rel32:
              self.DoPutChecked(LAt, LTarget - (LSite + 4), ADAM_LINKER_REL32_LOW,
                ADAM_LINKER_REL32_HIGH, 4);
            RelocKind.Rva32:
              self.DoPutChecked(LAt, LTarget, 0, ADAM_LINKER_RVA32_HIGH, 4);
            RelocKind.Abs64:
              PutLe(self.FBytes, LAt, uint64(self.DoImageBase() + LTarget), 8);
            RelocKind.SecRel32:
              self.DoPutChecked(LAt, LTarget - self.DoImageStartOf(LReloc.Symbol), 0,
                ADAM_LINKER_RVA32_HIGH, 4);
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The .pdata group's pieces (Adam's .pdata and a foreign object's), in the order laid out
    // (ascending offsets: a key is the offset above the id)
    hidden const method DoPdataPieces(): Int64Array;
    var
      LPieces: Int64Array;
      LId: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LK: int64;
    begin
      LCount := 0;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        if self.DoGroupOf(self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).GroupName) = ADAM_LINKER_PDATA then
          setlength(LPieces, LCount + 1);
          LPieces[LCount] := self.FSectionOffset[LId] * self.FSet.SectionCount + LId;
          LCount := LCount + 1;
        end;
      end;
      SortInt64s(LPieces);
      for LK := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LPieces[LK] := LPieces[LK] mod self.FSet.SectionCount;
      end;
      return LPieces;
    end;

    // LK0006 when the .pdata pieces are no run of whole entries laid end to end (a foreign
    // piece of another size, or a gap its alignment left); the table is then not written
    hidden method DoCheckExceptionTable();
    var
      LPieces: Int64Array;
      LK: int64;
      LExpect: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
    begin
      LPieces := self.DoPdataPieces();
      if len(LPieces) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LExpect := self.FSectionOffset[LPieces[0]];
      for LK := 0 to len(LPieces) - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LPieces[LK]);
        if ((LSection.Size() mod ADAM_LINKER_PDATA_ENTRY_SIZE) <> 0) or
          (self.FSectionOffset[LPieces[LK]] <> LExpect) then
          self.DoReport(ADAM_ERR_LINKER_006, 0, ADAM_MSG_LINKER_EXCEPTION_TABLE,
            NoArgs().Int(ADAM_LINKER_PDATA_ENTRY_SIZE).Str(LSection.SectionName));
          return;
        end;
        LExpect := LExpect + LSection.Size();
      end;
    end;

    // The exception table: the .pdata group's entries (one run, DoCheckExceptionTable) sorted
    // by their begin address (its first field), and its data directory; raises for a size that
    // is no whole number of entries
    hidden method DoExceptionTable();
    var
      LPieces: Int64Array;
      LId: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LB: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LKeys: Int64Array;
      LOld: ByteArray;
    begin
      LPieces := self.DoPdataPieces();
      if len(LPieces) = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LId := LPieces[0];
      LSize := 0;
      for LK := 0 to len(LPieces) - 1 do
        LSize := LSize + self.FSet.SectionAt(LPieces[LK]).Size();
      end;
      if LSize = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      if (LSize mod ADAM_LINKER_PDATA_ENTRY_SIZE) <> 0 then
        raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_PDATA + IntToStr(LSize) + " bytes");
      end;
      LCount := LSize div ADAM_LINKER_PDATA_ENTRY_SIZE;
      LAt := self.DoSectionFile(LId);
      // A key is the begin address (below 2 GB) above the entry's index: sorted keys give the
      // entries' new order, equal addresses kept in their order
      setlength(LKeys, LCount);
      setlength(LOld, LSize);
      for LK := 0 to LSize - 1 do
        LOld[LK] := self.FBytes[LAt + LK];
      end;
      for LK := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LKeys[LK] := (int64(GetLe(LOld, ADAM_LINKER_PDATA_ENTRY_SIZE * LK, 4)) shl 32) | LK;
      end;
      SortInt64s(LKeys);
      for LK := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LIndex := LKeys[LK] & ADAM_LINKER_LOW_32;
        for LB := 0 to ADAM_LINKER_PDATA_ENTRY_SIZE - 1 do
          self.FBytes[LAt + ADAM_LINKER_PDATA_ENTRY_SIZE * LK + LB] :=
            LOld[ADAM_LINKER_PDATA_ENTRY_SIZE * LIndex + LB];
        end;
      end;
      self.DoDirectory(ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_EXCEPTION, self.DoSectionRva(LId), LSize);
    end;

    // The Windows subsystem the image runs in: the GUI one for @subsystem gui, else the console
    hidden const method DoSubsystem(): int64;
    begin
      if self.FSettings.Gui then
        return ADAM_LINKER_SUBSYSTEM_WINDOWS_GUI;
      end;
      return ADAM_LINKER_SUBSYSTEM_WINDOWS_CUI;
    end;

    // The resources the settings ask for, in the directory's order (Adam.Coff.Resources): the
    // @exeicon file's images and group, then the version resource; their .rsrc bytes into
    // FResources (none: left empty). LK0007 at the @exeicon path for a file that cannot
    // be read or holds no icon
    hidden method DoResources();
    var
      LList: ImageResourceList;
      LIcon: ByteArray;
      LFault: IconFault;
      LTemplate: string;
    begin
      setlength(LList, 0);
      if self.FSettings.IconPath <> "" then
        if not ReadAllBytes(self.FSettings.IconPath, LIcon) then
          self.DoReport(ADAM_ERR_LINKER_007, self.FSettings.IconNode, ADAM_MSG_LINKER_ICON_READ,
            NoArgs().Str(self.FSettings.IconPath));
          return;
        end;
        LFault := IconResources(LIcon, LList);
        if LFault <> IconFault.None then
          LTemplate := ADAM_MSG_LINKER_ICON_PAST_END;
          if LFault = IconFault.NoDirectory then
            LTemplate := ADAM_MSG_LINKER_ICON_NO_DIRECTORY;
          end;
          if LFault = IconFault.NoImage then
            LTemplate := ADAM_MSG_LINKER_ICON_NO_IMAGE;
          end;
          self.DoReport(ADAM_ERR_LINKER_007, self.FSettings.IconNode, LTemplate,
            NoArgs().Str(self.FSettings.IconPath));
          return;
        end;
      end;
      if self.FSettings.VersionInfo then
        setlength(LList, len(LList) + 1);
        LList[len(LList) - 1] := VersionResource(self.FSettings);
      end;
      if len(LList) > 0 then
        self.FResources := ResourceSection(LList, self.FResourceFields);
      end;
    end;

    // The .rsrc bytes into its image section, each data entry's offset made an RVA (the
    // section's added), and its data directory
    hidden method DoResourceTable();
    var
      LImage: ref ImageSection;
      LK: int64;
      LField: int64;
    begin
      LImage := self.FImage[self.FResourceIndex];
      for LK := 0 to len(self.FResources) - 1 do
        self.FBytes[LImage.RawAt + LK] := self.FResources[LK];
      end;
      for LK := 0 to len(self.FResourceFields) - 1 do
        LField := LImage.RawAt + self.FResourceFields[LK];
        PutLe(self.FBytes, LField, GetLe(self.FBytes, LField, 4) + uint64(LImage.VirtualAddress), 4);
      end;
      self.DoDirectory(ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_RESOURCE, LImage.VirtualAddress, LImage.Size);
    end;

    // The file's bytes: headers, sections, import tables, relocations applied, the exception
    // table sorted, the resources, the base relocations
    hidden method DoWrite();
    var
      LReloc: ref ImageSection;
    begin
      setlength(self.FBytes, self.FFileSize);
      self.DoFileHeader();
      self.DoOptionalHeader();
      self.DoSectionTable();
      self.DoSectionBytes();
      if len(self.FLibraries) > 0 then
        self.DoImportTables();
      end;
      if self.FSettings.Dll then
        self.DoExportTable();
      end;
      self.DoRelocate();
      self.DoExceptionTable();
      if self.FResourceIndex >= 0 then
        self.DoResourceTable();
      end;
      if self.FTlsDirectory <> 0 then
        self.DoDirectory(ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_TLS, self.DoSectionRva(self.FTlsDirectory),
          ADAM_LINKER_TLS_DIRECTORY_SIZE);
      end;
      if self.FRelocIndex >= 0 then
        LReloc := self.FImage[self.FRelocIndex];
        self.DoBaseRelocs(LReloc.RawAt, true);
        self.DoDirectory(ADAM_LINKER_DIRECTORY_BASERELOC, LReloc.VirtualAddress, LReloc.Size);
      end;
    end;

    // The DLLs the exe imports, one per import directory entry, in its order (after Run)
    const method DllNames(): StringArray;
    var
      LNames: StringArray;
      LL: int64;
    begin
      setlength(LNames, len(self.FLibraries));
      for LL := 0 to len(self.FLibraries) - 1 do
        LNames[LL] := self.FLibraries[LL].DllName;
      end;
      return LNames;
    end;

    // The link (see the header): the exe's bytes, empty after a report
    method Run(): ByteArray;
    var
      LNone: ByteArray;
    begin
      self.DoThreadLocal();
      self.DoImportsFrom(1);
      self.DoLinkLibraries();
      // After a static library's report its symbols would only repeat it as LK0001
      if self.DoForeign() then
        self.DoDefinedImports();
        self.DoCRuntime();
        self.DoUndefined();
      end;
      if not self.FFailed then
        self.DoThreadCallbacks();
        self.DoEntry();
        self.DoExports();
        self.DoRemoveUnreached();
        self.DoResources();
      end;
      if not self.FFailed then
        self.DoPlan();
        self.DoLayout();
      end;
      if not self.FFailed then
        self.DoCheckExceptionTable();
      end;
      if self.FFailed then
        return LNone;
      end;
      self.DoWrite();
      return self.FBytes;
    end;
  end;

// ASections linked into a PE32+ exe for AMachine, entered at the symbol AEntry, the symbol
// AThreadCallback ("" none) the TLS directory's callback (DoThreadLocal), its imports'
// DLLs searched in ALibraryPaths (Adam.Coff.Exports.LibraryPaths), a static library's objects
// linked against ARuntime (the ABI's C runtime), reports at ATree's nodes into ADiagnostics
// (see the header); empty after a report. ADllNames: the DLLs the exe imports, in its import
// directory's order. ASettings: the subsystem and the resources the main module asks for
// (ExeSettings)
public routine LinkImage(const ASections: ref SectionSet; const AMachine: ref CoffMachine;
  const AEntry: string; const AThreadCallback: string; const ALibraryPaths: StringArray;
  const ARuntime: ref CRuntimeFacts; const ASettings: ref ExeSettings; const ATree: ref SyntaxTree;
  const ADiagnostics: ref Diagnostics; var ADllNames: StringArray): ByteArray;
var
  LLinker: ref CoffLinker;
  LBytes: ByteArray;
  LId: int64;
begin
  if (ASections = nil) or (AMachine = nil) or (ADiagnostics = nil) or (ARuntime = nil) or
    (ASettings = nil) then
    raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_INPUT);
  end;
  // An Info section is the compiler's data for an object file alone (Adam.Acu.*), never an
  // image's: one handed to the linker is a defect (a foreign object's is dropped as it is read)
  for LId := 1 to ASections.SectionCount - 1 do
    if ASections.SectionAt(LId).Kind = SectionKind.Info then
      raise(ADAM_LINKER_FAULT_INFO + ASections.SectionAt(LId).SectionName);
    end;
  end;
  LLinker := ref CoffLinker(ASections, AMachine, AEntry, AThreadCallback, ALibraryPaths, ARuntime,
    ASettings, ATree, ADiagnostics);
  LBytes := LLinker.Run();
  ADllNames := LLinker.DllNames();
  return LBytes;
end;

end.
